<title>POLAND: POLISH NET RESERVES INCH DOWN TO $21.46 FEB 1-20.</title>
<headline>POLISH NET RESERVES INCH DOWN TO $21.46 FEB 1-20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish official foreign</p>
<p>currency reserves eased by $9.6 million in February 1-20 to</p>
<p>$21.46 billion and were $202.8 million lower than at the start</p>
<p>of the year, preliminary National Bank of Poland figures</p>
<p>showed.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)  FEB 20     JAN  97   FEB 96</p>
<p>    Official reserves		 N/A	   N.A	17.01</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.46	 21.47     21.75</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves</p>
<p>are those held by the state. Net international reserves mean</p>
<p>the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking</p>
<p>system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
